 DemoCallbackErrors connected;F
⍝ An error in a callback must reach the application's ⎕TRAP as it does under
⍝ native ⎕DQ: an error escaping the callback's own frame - ⎕SIGNALled there, or
⍝ re-signalled by a handler cutting back to its caller, as GAMA's does -
⍝ surfaces at the line that called ⎕DQ, with ⎕DMX intact; an error deeper down
⍝ is trapped where it happened.
⍝
⍝ Each case runs twice. "Native" makes a native Timer's callback fail under a
⍝ native ⎕DQ; "EWC" opens a nested eDQ whose buttons' callbacks fail the same
⍝ way. Both callers localise the same ⎕TRAP, whose action (CBErrRec) reports in
⍝ F1.OUT what it sees: ⎕DMX, ⎕DM, how far above the DQ caller it ran, and in
⍝ which function. The two must match.
 EWC.CONNECTED←connected

 F←'F1'
 F eWC'Form' 'Callback Errors'(50 50)(120 460)('Coord' 'Pixel')
 (F,'.NATTOP')eWC'Button' 'Native: ⎕SIGNAL in callback'(12 12)(24 215)('Event' 'Select' 'CBErrNative')
 (F,'.NATDEEP')eWC'Button' 'Native: error deeper down'(12 233)(24 215)('Event' 'Select' 'CBErrNative')
 (F,'.EWC')eWC'Button' 'EWC: open a nested eDQ'(44 12)(24 215)('Event' 'Select' 'CBErrEwc')
 (F,'.CLEAR')eWC'Button' 'Clear'(44 233)(24 215)('Event' 'Select' 'CBErrClear')
 (F,'.OUT')eWC'Label' 'Click a button'(84 12)(22 436)
